Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: nested-YAML config fallback via targeted section
 extraction (v1.6)

Problem: PyYAML unavailable in the runtime container; the v1.2 fallback
parser rejected nested config.yaml, blocking plugin config load.

Solution (Approach B): extract only the secrets.vaultwarden section by
indentation tracking (_extract_nested_section), parse its scalar leaves
with a lenient flat parser (_parse_flat_mapping). Stdlib only.

- Add _indent_of, _clean_scalar, _parse_flat_mapping,
  _extract_nested_section, _fallback_parse_yaml
- Rewire _load_yaml_text to fall back when yaml import fails
- Remove _minimal_yaml_mapping nested-YAML rejection
- Update test_config_file_source_degrades_without_yaml (nested now succeeds)
- Add test_config_fallback_v16.py (real-world shape, siblings, URL colons)

No container changes. No config.yaml changes. No security changes.
